Carafe bench: the guest's FPCR keeps its floating-point trap enables off, as on the Cortex-A57.
The A57 ignores those bits; a host that implements them, such as the Snapdragon X, raised SIGFPE
in Eden's own code while the guest's FPCR was loaded.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes (0BSD in dynarmic's own notice).

diff --git a/src/dynarmic/src/dynarmic/backend/arm64/a64_interface.cpp b/src/dynarmic/src/dynarmic/backend/arm64/a64_interface.cpp
index c1c5891..81d0b29 100644
--- a/src/dynarmic/src/dynarmic/backend/arm64/a64_interface.cpp
+++ b/src/dynarmic/src/dynarmic/backend/arm64/a64_interface.cpp
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@ struct Jit::Impl final {
     }
 
     void SetFpcr(std::uint32_t value) {
-        current_state.fpcr = value;
+        current_state.fpcr = value & ~fpcr_trap_enables;
     }
 
     std::uint32_t Fpsr() const {
